  m_Name: item_l14_union_letter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GlorifiedBody.Interaction.ItemDefinition
  itemId: l14_union_letter
  displayName: A UNION LETTER
  kind: 1
  drugType: 0
  colour: {r: 0.96, g: 0.95, b: 0.88, a: 1}
  description: a union letter.
  logText: 'To the Fire Commissioner

    From the Executive Board


    Commissioner,


    My
    members did not sign up to carry grenade launchers. I have said it in your office
    and I am saying it on paper so nobody can say later that we didn''t.


    You
    bought them after the tower fire, when the ladders stopped at the ninth floor
    and nobody could get up the stairs. Fine. It worked that night. I was there,
    I will not pretend it didn''t.


    Since then the papers call us the army.
    The police department has asked three times to borrow them, and I would love
    to know for what. And a probationer, a kid in his first year who did exactly
    what the card on the case told him to do, put a canister through a window with
    a family behind it. He will carry that for the rest of his life. He should never
    have been carrying the other thing.


    No other department in the country
    does this. There is a reason for that, and it is not that we are braver.


    Take
    them back.


    The Executive Board'
  readFlag: 
  mapFloor: 
  audioClip: {fileID: 0}
  tapeLines: []
